#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:2
msgid "Contact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:4
msgid ""
"Contact the ROS community to ask for support, offer help, or suggest ways we "
"can improve. This article introduces the ways in which you can contact us."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:7
msgid ""
"**Area: community | content-type: about | experience: beginner, "
"intermediate, expert**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:10
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:13
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:15
msgid "You can contact the ROS community in the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:17
msgid ""
"`Stack Exchange <https://robotics.stackexchange.com/>`__: Ask for support or "
"discuss a problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:19
msgid ""
"Issue tracker: Submit an issue or suggest an enhancement: <Placeholder link "
"to new \"Submitting an issue\" article>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:21
msgid ""
":ref:`Discourse discussion boards <discussion-boards>`: Share ideas or "
"discuss best practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:23
msgid ""
"`Zulip chat <https://openrobotics.zulipchat.com/Recent>`_: Chat to other ROS "
"community members, including maintainers, in real time in the ``General`` or "
"``ROS General`` topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:25
msgid ""
"`Email <mailto:ros@openrobotics.org>`_: Contact us directly if you have a "
"private or sensitive issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:27
msgid ""
"`Email (security) <mailto:security@openrobotics.org>`_: Contact us directly "
"if you have a security concern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:32
msgid "Asking for support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:34
msgid ""
"Need help troubleshooting your system? First, search `Robotics Stack "
"Exchange <https://robotics.stackexchange.com/>`__ to see if others have had "
"similar problems, and if their solution works for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:37
msgid ""
"If not, ask a new question on `Robotics Stack Exchange <https://robotics."
"stackexchange.com/>`__. Make sure to add tags, at the very least the ``ros`` "
"tag and the distro version you are running, for example, ``rolling``. If "
"your question relates to the documentation, add a ``docs`` tag. You can also "
"add a tag for the relevant documentation area, for example, ``tutorials`` or "
"``concepts``. Please don't contact the developers/maintainers directly. The "
"community can't benefit from private answers and questions. Keep your "
"questions out in the public to help others with solving their problems. Open "
"Source development works best when the entire community participates in "
"discussions and helps to answer questions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:46
msgid ""
"If you can provide support to others, please do: <Placeholder link to new "
"Contributing to ROS article>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:51
msgid "Reporting an issue or suggesting an enhancement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:53
msgid ""
"If you identify issues, have suggestions for enhancements, or have a "
"question specific to one package, you can report an issue on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:55
msgid "<Placeholder link to new \"Reporting an issue\" article>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:59
msgid ""
"If you have a private or sensitive matter to discuss, email us directly at "
"`ros@openrobotics.org <mailto:ros@openrobotics.org>`__. If you have a "
"security concern, email us directly at `security@openrobotics.org <mailto:"
"security@openrobotics.org>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:65
msgid "Discussing ideas and best practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:67
msgid ""
"To start a discussion with other ROS community members, visit the official "
"`Open Robotics Discourse <https://discourse.openrobotics.org/>`_. Content on "
"Discourse should be discussions and announcements. It is not a place to get "
"*questions* about code answered, but it would be suitable to start a "
"conversation about new ideas, best practices, and improving standards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:71
msgid ""
"Discussions about ROS development and plans are also happening on the `Open "
"Robotics Discourse' ROS category <https://discourse.openrobotics.org/c/"
"ros/111>`_. Discussions about ROS are in the `ROS category <https://"
"discourse.openrobotics.org/c/ros/111>`_. Participating in these discussions "
"is an important way to have a say on how different features of ROS will work "
"and be implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:75
msgid ""
"The diverse community behind the ROS ecosystem is one of its greatest "
"assets. We encourage all members of the ROS community to participate in "
"these design discussions so that we can leverage the experience of community "
"members, and keep the varied use cases of ROS in mind when design decisions "
"are made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:79
msgid "Offering help"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:81
msgid ""
"If you are in a position to support others, share your knowledge and help "
"fellow users work through challenges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:83
msgid "<Placeholder link to new \"Contributing to ROS\" article>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:86
msgid "Contacting us privately"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:88
msgid ""
"If you'd like to contact us privately, for example, if your question "
"contains information sensitive to your organization or project, you can "
"email us directly at `ros@openrobotics.org <mailto:ros@openrobotics.org>`__. "
"If your message is regarding a security issue, email `security@openrobotics."
"org <mailto:security@openrobotics.org>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:92
msgid "Etiquette"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:94
msgid ""
"Assume 'good faith': It's easy to mis-interpret the meaning or tone of "
"comments on the internet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:95
msgid ""
"Assuming good faith gives the benefit of the doubt to those trying to help "
"you, avoiding insulting well-meaning community members and poisoning the "
"mood. Assuming 'good faith' when responding almost always works better, even "
"if the original response was not actually in good faith."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:98
msgid "Please don't send your question more than once: The question was seen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:99
msgid ""
"If you didn't get a response then likely nobody has had time to answer you. "
"Alternatively, it could be that nobody knows the answer. In any case, "
"sending it again is poor form and akin to shouting and is likely to "
"aggravate a large number of people. This also applies to cross-posting. Try "
"to pick the forum which you think matches best and ask there. If you are "
"referred to a new forum, provide a link to the old discussion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:106
msgid ""
"On `Robotics Stack Exchange <https://robotics.stackexchange.com/>`__ , you "
"can edit your question to provide more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:107
msgid ""
"The more details that you include in your question, the easier it is for "
"others to help you find your solution which makes it more likely for you to "
"get a response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:109
msgid "It's considered bad form to list your personal deadlines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:110
msgid "Community members answering questions also have them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:112
msgid "Do not beg for help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:113
msgid ""
"If there is someone willing and able to help with your problem, you usually "
"get a response. Asking for faster answers will mostly have a negative effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:116
msgid "Do not add unrelated content to posts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:117
msgid ""
"The content of posts should be focused on the topic at hand and not include "
"unrelated content. Content, links, and images unrelated to the topic are "
"considered spam."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:120
msgid ""
"For commercial posts, see also `this discussion <https://discourse."
"openrobotics.org/t/sponsorship-notation-in-posts-on-ros-org/2078>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:122
msgid "Minimize references to content behind pay walls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:123
msgid ""
"The content posted on Open Robotics Discourse and Robotics Stack Exchange "
"should be free and open to all users. Links to content behind pay walls such "
"as private journal articles, text books, and paid news websites, while "
"helpful and relevant, may not be accessible to all users. Where possible "
"primary sources should be free and open with paid content playing a "
"supporting role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:127
msgid "Single link posts are to be avoided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Contact.rst:128
msgid ""
"Generally speaking, posting a single link answer is less helpful and can be "
"easily confused with spam. Moreover, links may degrade over time or be "
"replaced. Paraphrasing a link's content along with some contextual "
"information and attribution is often much more helpful."
msgstr ""
